From 18237b19a1f7a2e957c40ecc0afbfcecf76c6414 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Muhomor <muhomor.dmitry@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 06:06:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/67] gmscompat: switch from RpcProvider to service bindings
 and broadcasts

Previously, service binders were provided through the RpcProvider in GmsCompat app. The previous
approach had the following issues, which are resolved with the new approach:
- calls from GmsCompat app to its clients failed when the clients were frozen
- GmsCompat app was killed before its clients in some cases
- GmsCore file proxy service was incompatible with persistent GmsCore process no longer being used
since 26.33.31 version

Additional changes:
- for GmsCore 26.33.31 and later, code that ran in the persistent GmsCore process now runs in the
main GmsCore process
- related improvements to the partial reimplementation of the android.provider.Settings API
- removal of unused code for limiting max allowed GmsCore and Play Store versions

(cherry picked from commit b75a554f7fff299349587a0b675e3b08132a32d8)
